WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.470
A second Riemann

00:00:01.282 --> 00:00:02.649
proof claim lands

00:00:03.174 --> 00:00:04.860
Mathematician Alessandro

00:00:04.672 --> 00:00:05.709
Masullo has a

00:00:05.521 --> 00:00:06.652
proposed proof of

00:00:06.464 --> 00:00:07.761
the Generalized Riemann

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:08.539
Hypothesis

00:00:08.646 --> 00:00:10.013
and Brian Conrad

00:00:09.825 --> 00:00:10.709
has been looking

00:00:10.521 --> 00:00:11.416
closely at it

00:00:11.228 --> 00:00:11.935
for months

00:00:12.124 --> 00:00:13.681
giving extensive feedback

00:00:13.551 --> 00:00:14.306
that is being

00:00:14.117 --> 00:00:15.072
incorporated

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:16.388
The hope was

00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:17.260
to bring Masullo

00:00:17.072 --> 00:00:18.015
to Stanford for

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:18.546
a year to

00:00:18.357 --> 00:00:19.489
polish the writing

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:20.574
then announce it

00:00:20.398 --> 00:00:21.281
after running it

00:00:21.093 --> 00:00:22.201
by enough people

00:00:22.718 --> 00:00:24.133
Instead the announcement

00:00:23.944 --> 00:00:24.911
came out hurried

00:00:24.994 --> 00:00:25.736
with a call

00:00:25.548 --> 00:00:26.302
for people to

00:00:26.114 --> 00:00:27.151
quickly check it

00:00:27.364 --> 00:00:28.319
formalize it

00:00:28.426 --> 00:00:29.616
and fill any

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:30.536
small gaps

00:00:31.062 --> 00:00:32.076
Full story on

00:00:31.887 --> 00:00:32.783
the dashboard
